{
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "heading", "text": "Variational Quantum Classifiers (VQC)", "level": 2 },
    { "type": "text", "body": "A **Variational Quantum Classifier** combines a parameterized quantum circuit (the ansatz) with a classical optimizer (like COBYLA or SPSA). The quantum circuit processes input features and outputs predicted probabilities, while the classical computer adjusts the variational parameters θ to minimize loss." },
    { "type": "callout", "variant": "tip", "body": "VQCs are key candidates for NISQ (Noisy Intermediate-Scale Quantum) devices because short circuit depths reduce error accumulation." },

    { "type": "heading", "text": "The Hybrid Training Loop", "level": 2 },
    { "type": "text", "body": "1. **Encoding:** Input vector x is encoded into the circuit via feature map gates U(x)." },
    { "type": "text", "body": "2. **Ansatz execution:** Parameterized gates V(θ) are applied to transform the state." },
    { "type": "text", "body": "3. **Measurement:** Expectation value ⟨Z⟩ is measured to compute predicted class probability P(y=1|x, θ)." },
    { "type": "text", "body": "4. **Classical update:** Loss function compute L(θ, y). Classical optimizer computes parameter update Δθ." },

    { "type": "heading", "text": "Basic VQC Ansatz Architecture", "level": 2 },
    { "type": "step_circuit", "numQubits": 2, "caption": "2-Qubit Variational Ansatz with Ry(θ) Rotations & CNOT Entanglement",
      "gates": [
        { "id": "vqc1", "gate": "RY", "qubits": [0], "column": 0, "param": 0.52 },
        { "id": "vqc2", "gate": "RY", "qubits": [1], "column": 0, "param": 1.28 },
        { "id": "vqc3", "gate": "CX", "qubits": [0, 1], "column": 1 },
        { "id": "vqc4", "gate": "RZ", "qubits": [0], "column": 2, "param": -0.84 },
        { "id": "vqc5", "gate": "RZ", "qubits": [1], "column": 2, "param": 0.41 }
      ],
      "stepDescriptions": [
        "Initial encoded state |ψ(x)⟩",
        "Layer 1: Parameterized Ry rotations on all qubits",
        "Entangling CNOT gate to correlate parameters across qubits",
        "Layer 2: Parameterized Rz rotations to tune quantum phase"
      ]
    },

